 "signs": [
  {
   "x": 25,
   "y": 11,
   "text": "THE NEW FOOTBRIDGE, 2019. Two cantilevers that almost touch, with a 4 cm gap in the middle. It replaced a steep stair, and the gap is a design feature, not a mistake."
  },
  {
   "x": 8,
   "y": 7,
   "text": "GALLOS. A giant bronze-coloured king standing on the headland since 2016. 'Gallos' is Cornish for 'power'. He looks out to sea as if he's expecting someone."
  },
  {
   "x": 15,
   "y": 11,
   "text": "TINTAGEL CASTLE. Sixth-century fortress, 13th-century castle. Geoffrey of Monmouth says King Arthur was conceived here. The castle sniffs, and says Arthur was born whenever it suited the tourist board."
  },
  {
   "x": 12,
   "y": 27,
   "text": "MERLIN'S CAVE. A sea cave right through the headland, 100 m long, reached at low tide. Legend says it's where Merlin found baby Arthur. On a good tide, the sea does the rest of the story."
  },
  {
   "x": 32,
   "y": 19,
   "text": "TINTAGEL. A tiny village with a big myth. Tintagel is Cornish 'Din Tagell', the fort of the narrow neck. A very good name for a place with only one way in."
  },
  {
   "x": 37,
   "y": 40,
   "text": "ST MATERIANA'S CHURCH. A Norman cliff church, nearly a thousand years old. Materiana was a Welsh saint. The church survived a thousand winters, and never complained about the wind."
  },
  {
   "x": 9,
   "y": 13,
   "plaque": "tintagel_tristan",
   "title": "Tristan and Iseult",
   "text": "In the medieval romance, Tintagel is the court of King Mark of Cornwall. His nephew Tristan fetches Iseult from Ireland to be Mark's bride, they drink a love potion by mistake, and it ends in tears. Near Fowey an old stone bears the name Drustanus."
  },
  {
   "x": 49,
   "y": 16,
   "plaque": "tintagel_boscastle_flood",
   "title": "Boscastle Flood",
   "text": "Just up the coast, on 16 August 2004, a cloudburst sent a flash flood roaring through Boscastle and swept cars out to sea. Helicopters lifted about a hundred people to safety, and remarkably nobody died. The village rebuilt, and its witchcraft museum reopened."
  }
 ],
